indic_normalizer
================

This product includes software and/or data derived from third-party projects.
It has no runtime dependency on them; the relevant material was vendored and
adapted into this repository.

1. AI4Bharat / indic-numtowords
   - Source: https://github.com/AI4Bharat/indic-numtowords
   - License: MIT
   - Use: The number-to-words tables and cardinal conversion logic for the 22
     scheduled Indian languages (+ English) were vendored (with minor import
     adaptation) into `indic_normalizer/numbers/_numengine/`. Cardinal readings
     are produced by this vendored engine.

2. Kenpath Technologies / indic-text-normalization
   - Source: https://github.com/Kenpath/indic-text-normalization
   - License: Apache-2.0
   - Use: Only its semiotic-class taxonomy (cardinal, ordinal, decimal,
     fraction, date, time, telephone, measure, money, electronic, roman,
     abbreviation, whitelist) informed the design of this project's
     rule-based handlers. No code from this project is included; in particular
     this project does NOT use pynini / WFST.

All other code (preprocessing, class handlers, year/decimal/ordinal readers,
the LaTeX-to-speech engine, and packaging) is original to this project and
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
